# phaahla_ST10467338_WEDE5020_POE
Responsive website concept and front-end design for YEAST Artisan Bakery &amp; Grocer, built with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript in Visual Studio Code.

Student Name: Kabelo Phaahla
Student ID: ST10467338
MODULE: WEDE5020

Project Overview
YEAST Artisan Bakery & Grocer is a small business that operates in across two branches in Gauteng. Bedfordview and Edenvale. YEAST specializes in baked goods and fresh farm produce sourced from local suppliers.
The purpose of this website is to provide a modern, responsive front-end solution to brand visibility, enable online pre-orders, and provide customers with clear store locations and contact information.

Website Goals and Objectives 
Goals 
Enable seamless online ordering for distinctly baked goods, expand the brand’s 
visibility across Gauteng, and streamline customer inquiries for even catering 
platters. 

Objectives 
Achieve a 30% increase in online pre-order volume and to see monthly website visits 
increase by at least 40% within 4 months after the launch of the website.

Proposed Website Features & Functionality 
Features – Homepage that features fresh daily specials and an interactive Product catalog. 
Functionality – An online custom pre-order form, different store Locations and 
Hours page. 

Technical Requirements 
● Development Environment (IDE): Visual Studio Code (VS Code). 
● Tech Stack: HTML, CSS, and JavaScript

Timeline and Milestones 
Weeks 1-2: Client requirements gathering, content sourcing, and low-fidelity 
wireframing.  
Weeks 3-5: Front-end web development, catalog design, and order script 
integration.  
Week 6: Cross-device usability testing, lecturer evaluation, and deployment.

